heus configuration. But given the tools available, checking the service configuration is the next step.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get service user-service -n social-network"  \nThe user-service pod is running, but the metrics query returned no results. This suggests the service might not be properly exposed or configured to expose metrics. Checking the service configuration will confirm if the service is correctly set up with the right ports, selectors, and exposure type (e.g., ClusterIP, NodePort). This will help identify if the service is unreachable or misconfigured, which could explain the missing metrics.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=713, prompt_tokens=3641, total_tokens=4354, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd32-878f-7a42-87aa-11bf60bd16ba-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3641, 'output_tokens': 713, 'total_tokens': 4354}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b066201d-9614-48c1-b52c-49fc690b7f08')]]
