leading to no endpoints. That would explain why the metrics aren\'t being scraped. So the next step is to describe the pod to check its labels and see if they match the service\'s selector.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl describe pod user-service-559b79c875-gcl2q -n social-network"  \nThe service `user-service` has no endpoints, meaning no pods match its selector. To diagnose this, I need to check the pod\'s labels to confirm if they align with the service\'s selector (`service=user-service`). If the pod lacks this label, the service cannot route traffic to it, resulting in missing metrics and potential connectivity issues.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 339, 'prompt_tokens': 4248, 'total_tokens': 4587, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd32-fbb2-7e32-85f8-130a625ba6ee-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4248, 'output_tokens': 339, 'total_tokens': 4587}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='19fd5c60-15cd-4474-9599-d6b90f8ff071'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user-service service has no endpoints, which means the pods it\'s supposed to route traffic to aren\'t matching the selector. The service\'s selector is "service=user-service", so I need to check the pod\'s labels.\n\nThe pod in question is user-service-559b79c875-gcl2q. I should describe this pod to look at its labels. If the pod doesn\'t have the label "service=user-service", that\'s the problem. The service can\'t find pods with the right selector, so endpoints are empty. \n\nI\'ll use kubectl describe pod to get the details. Once I check the labels, I can confirm if the pod is correctly labeled. If not, that\'s the root cause. If it is, maybe there\'s another issue, like the pod not being ready or a different configuration problem. But the main thing here is the label mismatch.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod user-service-559b79c875-gcl2q -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b036e9cd9c67aa9c', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 240, 'prompt_tokens': 5255, 'total_tokens': 5495, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd33-0baa-73b3-aecd-a82365053dc6-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod user-service-559b79c875-gcl2q -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b036e9cd9c67aa9c', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5255, 'output_tokens': 240, 'total_tokens': 5495}), ToolMessage(content='Name:             user-service-559b79c875-gcl2q\nNamespace:        social-network\nPriority:         0\nService Account:  default\nNode:             node1.htliang2-agent.insai-pg0.apt.emulab.net/128.110.96.32\nStart Time:       Tue, 17 Mar 2026 19:05:29 +0000\nLabels:           app=user-service\n                  pod-template-hash=559b79c875\n                  service=user-service\nAnnotations:      <none>\nStatus:           Running\nIP:               10.244.1.236\nIPs:\n  IP:           10.244.1.236\nControlled By:  ReplicaSet/user-service-559b79c875\nContainers:\n  user-service:\n    Container ID:  docker://75b3d59f16f66843aafa78416118bed073096311c97295a74fd22ab1b457a8bb\n    Image:         docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest\n   