o see if there are more to undo. \n\nBut the user\'s current step is to generate the tool call. Since they chose rollback_command, the correct tool call is to execute it. The arguments are empty, as per the function definition. So the tool call should be {"name": "rollback_command", "arguments": {}}. \n\nBut the user has to make sure that they are rolling back the correct commands. If they have a list from get_previous_rollbackable_cmd, they should process each one in reverse order. However, the rollback_command tool automatically handles the order by undoing the last executed command first. So each call to rollback_command undoes the most recent one. \n\nTherefore, the correct action here is to call rollback_command again. The user might need to do this multiple times until all changes are reverted. But in this step, they just need to make the tool call for rollback_command.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'rollback_command'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-80e1ce4d237ebb6b', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 464, 'prompt_tokens': 1249, 'total_tokens': 1713, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd37-7749-7202-b80b-4f57617d7414-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'rollback_command', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-80e1ce4d237ebb6b', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1249, 'output_tokens': 464, 'total_tokens': 1713}), ToolMessage(content='No more actions to rollback., action_stack: ActionStack: [Empty]', id='567f2afa-2d74-4130-ae2c-21662f4a9e68', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-80e1ce4d237ebb6b'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.'