itional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1181, 'prompt_tokens': 3376, 'total_tokens': 4557, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd37-ddaa-7d63-bd72-5ba17b1c0bb0-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3376, 'output_tokens': 1181, 'total_tokens': 4557}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0335598e-bd71-4cbc-85dd-664eb10ff345'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me think. The user is trying to figure out why the user-service can't connect to user-mongodb. They've already checked the pods and services, and everything seems up. The next step was to test connectivity directly to the MongoDB pod's IP. The previous attempt used `nc` but got an error about interactive commands. So, I need to adjust the command to be non-interactive.\n\nWait, the tool's description says interactive commands are not supported. The previous command used `-it` which is interactive. So, I should remove the `-it` flag to make it non-interactive. Let me try using `nc -zv` without the interactive flags. That should work. Let me check the syntax again. The correct command would be `kubectl exec -n social-network -it user-service-0 -- nc -zv 10.244.1.230 27017` but without the `-it` to avoid interactivity. Wait, no, the `-it` is for interactive terminal. Maybe the tool doesn't support that. So, the correct command should be `kubectl exec -n social-network user-service-0 -- nc -zv 10.244.1.230 27017` without the `-it` to make it non-interactive. That should work. Let me make sure the command is formatted correctly as a single string. Also, ensure the pod name is correct. The user mentioned the MongoDB pod is at 1